ZooTasks

Professional Task Marketplace & Earning Platform

ZooTasks is a Django-powered task marketplace platform designed to connect task creators and task workers. Users can explore tasks, complete work, manage their wallets, and participate in promotions and offers.

Features

User registration and authentication

User dashboard

Task marketplace and task submission

Task management and administration

Wallet and transaction management

Withdrawal request management

Promotions and offers

Django admin panel

Telegram bot integration

Responsive web interface

Technology Stack

Backend: Python, Django

Database: SQLite for local development

Frontend: HTML, CSS, Django Templates

Bot: Python Telegram Bot integration

Deployment: Configured for web hosting and deployment workflows

Project Structure

zootasks/ ├── backend/ │ ├── accounts/ │ ├── config/ │ ├── core/ │ ├── main/ │ ├── offers/ │ ├── promotions/ │ ├── tasks/ │ ├── wallet/ │ ├── manage.py │ └── requirements.txt ├── Dockerfile ├── docker-compose.yml ├── railway.json ├── build.sh └── README.md 

Local Development

1. Clone the repository

git clone https://github.com/Rafiqual69/Zootasks.git cd Zootasks 

2. Create and activate a virtual environment

python -m venv venv source venv/bin/activate 

3. Install dependencies

cd backend pip install -r requirements.txt 

4. Configure environment variables

Create a .env file and add your local configuration, Django secret key, and other required settings.

Never commit secrets, passwords, or API tokens to GitHub.

5. Run migrations

python manage.py migrate 

6. Create an admin account

python manage.py createsuperuser 

7. Start the development server

python manage.py runserver 

Open the website at:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/ 

Admin panel:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/ 

Project Status

ZooTasks is under active development. Features, user interfaces, and backend functionality may continue to evolve.

Security

Keep .env files private.

Do not expose production credentials.

Use strong passwords for administrator accounts.

Review configuration before deploying publicly.

